The files of this folder that come from the Icon program library (packs/ibpag2 of the Icon distribution, version 9.5.25a) are in the public domain.
The README of the Icon distribution says:

    This material is in the public domain.  You may use and copy this material
    freely.  This privilege extends to modifications, although any modified
    version of this system given to a third party should clearly identify your
    modifications as well as the original source.

    The responsibility for the use of this material resides entirely with you.
    We make no warranty of any kind concerning this material, nor do we make
    any claim as to the suitability of Icon for any application.

THE ORIGINAL SOURCE: the Icon program library, packs/ibpag2 (Ibpag2, an LR-based parser generator in Icon, by Richard L. Goerwitz).
OUR MODIFICATIONS, in the fifteen .icn files and nowhere else: one line is added to ibpag2.icn, link slshupto, rewrap, outbits, sortff, itokens, slrtbls, slritems, follow, ibutil, iohno, ibreader, ibwriter, shrnktbl, version (the fourteen files the pack's Makefile hands the translator beside it); tab characters are written as spaces (columns of eight), and a semicolon is written at the
end of every statement, as SCRIP's Icon and the fleet's Icon translator require. No other byte is changed. The README beside this file says how and how it
was proved.
